<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Banu Khattab emirate</h1><p class="st-meta">918 CE – 1172 CE (approx.) · capital Zawila</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Berber Ibadi dynasty of the Fezzan, ruling the Saharan slave-trade town of Zawila for over two centuries.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zawila">Zawila</a>, in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-fezzan">Fezzan</a> of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a>, lay in the former lands of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/garamantian-empire">Garamantian Empire</a>. Around 918 Abd <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allah">Allah</a> ibn al-Khattab of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hawwara">Hawwara</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berbers</a> established the dynasty there, controlling oases on the main caravan route between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-chad">Lake Chad</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Banu Khattab were Ibadi Muslims who ruled a network of oases from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zawila">Zawila</a>, which Arab geographers describe as a walled town with a mosque and markets. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> grew rich from the trade in enslaved people brought from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-kanem">Kanem</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-chad">Lake Chad</a> region, exchanged for horses, textiles and metal goods, and from date cultivation.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1172 to 1176 <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/qaraqushs-tripolitania">Sharaf al-Din Qaraqush</a>, a commander serving the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubid Empire</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a>, invaded the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-fezzan">Fezzan</a> and killed the last Khattabid ruler. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fezzan">Fezzan</a> later came under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-kanem">Kanem</a> and local dynasties.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="emirate, 918 CE – 1172 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">emirate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:77.97%;width:5.05%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>918 CE – 1172 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Zawila</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abd Allah ibn al-Khattab</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ibadi Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Berber, Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/libya">Libya</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Banu al-Khattab, Emirate of Zawila</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1045&amp;focus=banu-khattab-emirate" aria-label="Banu Khattab emirate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5151 1203 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Banu Khattab emirate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5343 1461h0M5811 1337h0M5338 1239h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5471 1459h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5471 1459h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Libya. <a href="/atlas?year=1045&amp;focus=banu-khattab-emirate">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
